      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your premise is a bold one, but you'll need to be careful not to dismiss legitimate concerns as mere \"fallacies.\" For the first section, categorize arguments like job displacement as *misallocative concerns*, arguing they fail to account for the long-term, aggregate productivity gains from specialization. Then, frame arguments against free trade as *short-sighted risk assessments*, showing how they ignore the systemic benefits of global supply chains. Finally, conclude by asserting that while localized pain is real, it is an acceptable externality in the pursuit of maximized global welfare, which is the only metric that matters in modern economic modeling.",
      "source": "target",
